00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.860
Code number confirmed.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.760
Please reroute to Gate 5.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.990
What are you talking about?
We're the Lovely Angels.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:46.500
Hurry up and open the gate.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.030
This gate is currently closed.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.110
Please use Gate 5.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.340
Look, you're really starting to piss me off.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.930
You wanna get scrapped?

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.570
Kei, you might not want to do that.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.780
I'm not sure what's going on, but let's go.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.850
Stupid machine...

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.520
Just calm down.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.930
There's an emergency situation, so
everyone is getting rerouted to Gate 5.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.490
What kind of an emergency?

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.400
Well, the Research and Development
Division has been working on...

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.700
...a new type of security system called Algernon,

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.070
and its classified data has been stolen.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.900
That's why you called us back?

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.300
Exactly.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.640
Fortunately, we discovered the theft
early enough to seal off all the buildings...

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.640
...before the culprit could escape.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.500
A break-in where they're
making the security system?

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.050
So much for tight security.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.480
Enough with the sarcasm.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.690
The head of the Research and Development
Division specifically requested you two...

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.380
...to solve this matter.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:45.290
Eh? Chief Fangoria did?

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.590
So do we have an idea who the culprit is?

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.660
We don't.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.970
What we do know is that the
classified data hasn't been taken...

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.940
...out of the 3WA building yet.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.770
What do you think?

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.570
That old woman can be real scary
when she doesn't get her way.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.560
Will you approve what
we've been discussing then?

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.910
We were making friends with some gorgeous
hunks when you called us back, you know.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.120
I get your point. You'll get a special bonus.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.050
And a special extra week of vacation, right?

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.750
I never agreed to that.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.620
Oh, is that so?

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.390
Let's go home, shall we?

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:15.880
Yes, lets.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:18.920
W-Wait!

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.860
Special vacation?

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.020
One week?

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.530
F-Fine.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:24.960
I'll make a special exception.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.340
All right! Now that that's settled,
let's wrap this up quickly.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.000
Yeah.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.210
We know the culprit is inside the building.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.470
This will be a piece of cake.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.010
Th-The Dirty Pair!

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.570
We're doomed.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.410
The headquarters is doomed!

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.640
I'd better go home and evacuate.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.450
I sent the Dirty Pair your way.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.550
Are you really sure about this?

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.520
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.190
They're the only ones who can do this job.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.230
I'm more concerned about the
safety of our headquarters.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.120
I won't be held responsible for any of this.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.860
I'll take full responsibility.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:58.890
It won't affect you.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:05.610
I'll keep a close eye on them,
so you have nothing to worry about.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:24.890
The Little Dictator!
Let Sleeping Top Secrets Lie

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:32.100
Does all this junk really sell?

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.970
Slap a 3WA label on it and they
sell like hotcakes, apparently.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.440
Seriously, I can't imagine what people
are thinking when they make this stuff.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:40.440
What's this?

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.450
People can't help but touch the peculiar
ring that's hanging in the middle of the room.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:55.080
So, how do you like our human trap
that utilizes that basic instinct?

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.520
This isn't funny, Chief!

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.530
Blame yourself for falling for it.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.490
That's what you get for calling our products junk.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:05.430
What a witch.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:06.600
Tell me about it.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.970
Just so you know, I have excellent hearing,

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.460
so watch what you say.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.670
Yes, Ma'am. We understand.
Yes, Ma'am. We understand.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.170
Stop right there!

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:16.910
What are you doing?

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:17.840
Professor?

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:19.550
Fangoria! It's terrible!

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.050
Lice Mk. 1 has escaped!

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:21.920
Let go of me!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.150
You fool! Don't move!

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.620
Move and you'll become an idiot!

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.190
Calm down!

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.160
Kei, do something!

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:29.890
Be quiet!

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:31.120
Stay away!

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.090
Ah, right...

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.020
Hold still.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:35.890
A flea?

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:39.600
That was close.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.600
One second more and you would have
turned into a complete bimbo.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.660
What do you mean?

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:47.900
Your brain cells get completely
destroyed if you get bit by Lice Mk. 1.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.800
Could it have been an inside job?

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.580
All of my staff are trustworthy.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:58.050
That's not too convincing when you have a
weirdo professor like him hanging around.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.650
It doesn't matter who the culprit is.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.060
All we care about is getting Algernon back.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:06.590
So Chief, this "Algernon"...

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.160
What kind of security system is it?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.190
That's none of your concern!

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.170
How are we supposed to find it
if you don't tell us what we're looking for?

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:18.670
Algernon is equipped with a special transmitter.

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.940
All you need to do is use this
tracker to follow its signal.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.070
If you don't like it, I can always get someone else.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.510
However, I thought your special
bonus was contingent on this job?

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.350
Funny, I don't recall ever
saying we didn't want to do it.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.790
Sheesh, who'd want to turn
into an old witch like her?

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.690
The target is currently on level B2.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.420
Don't you think they're being awfully
generous for such an easy job?

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:48.070
I bet it's got something to do with this "Algernon."

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:52.170
What is Algernon?

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.370
Cannot answer.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:56.940
What do you mean?

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:01.510
Special order 937, for Chief Fangoria's eyes only.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.880
Just ignore that witch's orders.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.310
Cannot ignore.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.490
Why you stubborn little!

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:06.890
It's no use getting angry.
Why you stubborn little!

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:07.720
It's no use getting angry.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.120
Let me handle this.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:12.920
Come on, Brain, do us a favor and tell us.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.520
I cannot answer, no matter
how many times you ask.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.000
Don't be so cold.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.970
If you want to be popular with the girls,
you need to be more reasonable.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:21.930
Does not compute.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:23.840
It's hopeless.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.340
This calls for a lesson.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:27.070
Take that!
Take that!

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:30.140
There!

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.940
Don't you think you overdid it a bit?

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:57.870
Two weeks' vacation!

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.170
Double our bonus!

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.340
Two weeks' vacation!

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.710
Double our bonus!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:05.970
It's so annoying that we have to do
whatever that old hag tells us to do.

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:07.910
We totally deserve two weeks' vacation for it.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.420
We're close.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.280
My, how cute!

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.050
What's wrong with you?

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.580
Oh, long time no see.

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:52.160
Oh, no!

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:55.860
A cat that's scared of mice...

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:58.000
I bet Mughi's ancestors
are rolling over in their graves.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.030
Genetic engineering works
in mysterious ways, doesn't it?

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.540
The most important thing is a pristine kitchen,
but they keep finding their way in somehow.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.540
Why are there mice in this building?

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:11.670
Mice are hard to get rid of.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:15.310
They always find a way to get in.
It's a fact of nature.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:21.720
Oh, that's right.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:25.180
There's still some of your
favorite almond tofu left over.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.900
Want some?

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:27.860
Definitely!

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.630
I thought you were on a diet?

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.130
No worries there.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:36.030
This almond tofu is made from
vegetable protein, so you won't get fat.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.710
What's going on?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.170
This has never happened in all
five thousand years of Chinese history!

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.490
By the way, where did Mughi and Nanmo go?

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:27.110
They took off without us!

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:33.850
Not again!
Not again!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.550
Emergency situation.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:07.150
Emergency situation.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:09.360
Area BC of the main building has been sealed off.

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:12.290
I repeat, area BC of the main
building has been sealed off.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:13.790
Emergency situation.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.560
All non-security personnel should
evacuate the building immediately.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:20.060
Huh?

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.700
So "Algernon" is a mouse, Professor?

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.370
Yes, that is correct.

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:30.840
Is this Algernon?

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:33.310
No, this is Chichi.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.840
Where did Al go?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:37.890
The mouse talked!

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:40.680
This mouse has an IQ of 135.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:41.480
Huh?

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:44.690
And Algernon has an IQ of 153.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:47.700
Chichi, Algernon will be back soon.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.790
An IQ of 153?!

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:51.520
It's higher than yours, Yuri.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.700
Mine is 156, thank you!

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.660
You don't look it, though.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:01.380
We were experimenting with the beta-carboline
alkaloids extracted from Lice Mk. 1,

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.650
and the lab mice's brain capacities
increased significantly.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.840
Those mice were later named
Algernon and Chichi.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.850
They're my neuroscience masterpiece.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.750
Using these genius mice,

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.950
we planned to create the most powerful
security system in the universe.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:17.820
Basically, mice exist on every planet now.

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:21.190
Algernon can control those mice
and make them aggressive.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:23.870
Algernon can also command those
mice to prohibit any human...

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.270
...from getting their hands on
any top secret information.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:29.670
So, Aljarnon can command ordinary mice
and turn them into a military unit?

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:30.370
Exactly.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:32.670
Mice can get into every nook and cranny.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:35.440
They also have an explosive reproductive rate.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:40.620
So basically, you called us in to test your
genius mouse's ability as a commander?

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:41.270
Indeed.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:45.390
It's to see if Algernon can protect
itself against 3WA's worst...

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:49.060
Er, top agents.
That is the goal of this experiment.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:53.220
What do you mean by "worst," Miss Fang...
er, Chief Fangoria?

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:56.020
You two have a reputation for being reckless.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.360
The more reckless, the better
with this experiment.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.300
Is that supposed to be a compliment?

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.630
Take it any way you like.

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:09.410
Algernon?

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:10.630
Listen up.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.240
I am taking control of this building.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:14.970
All humans leave immediately.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.250
What's gotten into you?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.910
W-Why are you doing this?

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:33.960
Chichi, come back!

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:01.330
A-All of the city mice are flooding
into the 3WA Headquarters!

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:02.990
At this rate, the headquarters will be!

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:08.200
You guys made this problem, so you solve it.

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.140
Not so fast.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:12.400
Lovely Angels, this is an emergency order!

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:13.970
Get this ruckus under control somehow!

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:15.840
Triple bonus!

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.940
Three weeks' vacation!

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:47.140
Don't underestimate me!

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:47.540
Whoa!

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:00.950
Go for it!

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:02.950
Open!

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:08.890
Go get those mice!

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.160
I brought you something!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:10.990
Catch!

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:15.540
The enemy is operating out of
the food storage units.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.140
How's Brain?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.840
The main computer is safe, but its terminals
have been taken over, so it has its hands full.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:33.990
Okay, let's go get 'em!

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:34.650
Let's go!

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.440
Hey! They're all a bunch of 'fraidy-cats?

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:00.110
Absolutely not!

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:02.770
You can't kill Algernon or Chichi!

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:05.780
What other option do we have?
We have to gas them.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:08.610
Do you have any idea how much
we spent on their development?

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:10.830
Then are you just going to hand
the 3WA Headquarters over to them?

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:12.590
I'll convince Algernon.

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:14.160
Get with the program already.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:15.030
What?

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.930
Algernon revolted against you because
he got tired of being used by you.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.800
Yeah... Don't you get it?

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:23.840
But if I show just how much I love them...

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:28.370
Listen, all intelligent beings eventually
grow tired of taking orders from idiots.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:29.510
What are you looking at?

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:32.640
We had Brain look up some old data.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:36.520
According to this, Professor Gessy's IQ is 125.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:38.320
And Chief Fangoria is...

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:38.650
Enough!
And Chief Fangoria is...

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:39.020
Enough!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.760
Well, in any case,

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:48.100
it was a foolish idea to create mice
that are smarter than their keepers.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:50.730
The mice know they're smarter than you,

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:52.720
so your so-called love
won't mean a thing to them.

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:54.370
Plus, if you use poison gas,

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.360
it'll put this building
out of commission completely.

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:58.270
Then, what do you suggest we do?

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.170
Old fashioned hand-to-hand combat, that's what!

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:02.110
But it's going to cost you extra, Chief!

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.110
We have no other choice.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:06.770
My department will cover it.

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:07.980
As it should.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:08.970
It's settled then!

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:17.390
From here on, it's mice country, huh?

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:18.690
Do you think we'll need our passports?

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:21.260
Killer mice!

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:23.290
Here we go!

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:28.330
I hope this thing works!

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.730
Are you really planning to use that?

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:33.070
An eye for an eye!

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:35.170
We're pitting Lice Mk. 1
against that genius mouse!

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:38.010
We could be the ones who end
up stupid big time, you know.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.000
Then so be it. Our daily woes will
all go away in an instant!

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.830
It's going to take a lot
more than that to hit us.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:10.570
Yuri!

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:23.650
Take that!

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:36.670
Not again!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:39.100
Why does this always have to happen...

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:40.340
Mughi!

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:53.180
I've been bitten!

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:57.080
Stay away! I said, stay away!

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:01.560
To the great mouse ancestors,

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:04.930
I present to you this giant
sacrificial cat on this glorious day!

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.070
Stop it already!

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:08.190
What is this? A new cult or something?

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:10.530
Yuri!

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:11.730
Get a hold of yourself!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:16.870
It feels good when Lice Mk. 1 bites you...

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:22.680
Who am I?

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:23.810
Where am I?

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:48.040
Nanmo!
Nanmo!

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:51.200
All right!
All right!

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.050
We were bitten by an ordinary flea!

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.820
This is the real Lice Mk. 1!

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:09.820
Guess this proves Yuri's IQ is
three points higher than yours!

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:17.600
Chichi!

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:22.880
It's coming this way!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:23.180
Stay away!
It's coming this way!

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:23.670
Stay away!

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:25.070
Wait!

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:29.380
Ow!

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:34.750
Hey, at least you weren't
bitten, right? I saved you.

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:50.200
It committed suicide...

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:52.440
They say mice are stubborn creatures, but...

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:54.670
...they're quite fragile when they're
too intelligent, aren't they?

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:56.710
Guess being too smart
isn't that great either, huh?

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:59.800
Chichi, you're happy you're back to
being an ordinary mouse, right?

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:03.680
From now on you live out your life
as an ordinary mouse, okay?

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:49.830
The mystery began after I fell asleep that time
Ano toki nemuri no ato ni okotta mistuerii

00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:56.300
I was guided by a voice from the future
Mirai kara kuru koe ni michibikareta no yo

00:22:56.300 --> 00:23:02.810
I passed through a distant, silvery time tunnel
Giniro haruka na taimu tonneru nukete

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:09.480
And met a wanderer with unclouded eyes
Deatta sunda me no samayoibito

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:11.890
Space Fantasy

00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:16.190
I came all this way just to meet you
Anata ni ai ni kokomade kita no

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:18.390
Space Fantasy

00:23:18.390 --> 00:23:22.260
I came all this way just to meet you
Anata ni ai ni kokomade kita no

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:28.740
Even if you were from another planet,
Tatoeba anata ga betsu no hoshi no hito demo

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:35.110
It wouldn't matter to me, because I've fallen in love
Watashi wa kamawanai aishita nara

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:39.010
Dirty, Stormy Destiny

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.750
Dirty, Stormy Destiny

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:48.180
Love is zero G...
Koi wa mujuuryoku...

00:24:01.400 --> 00:24:02.800
W-What's wrong, Yuri?

00:24:02.870 --> 00:24:04.940
It was just a dream... Thank goodness...

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:06.800
It was really that scary?

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:10.340
A narrow and dark sewer system...

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:13.410
Mushy-gushy monsters...

00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:14.140
Huh?

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:16.950
Oh, no! I don't think
that was just a dream! Look!

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:17.510
Urp!

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:18.580
The next episode is...

00:24:18.650 --> 00:24:21.750
"What's This?! My Supple Skin Is a Mess!"

